        "original_id": "f5c8d0cd-049d-5f22-8cf0-0e0bed834cb9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Tennis Court\", \"Royals\", \"Mother Mother\"\n- People: Lorde\n- Companies: Universal Music Group\n- Albums and EPs: \"Pure Heroine\", \"The Love Club EP\"\n- Charts: Billboard Alternative Songs\n\nFacts:\n- In 2012, Lorde released \"Royals\" on her debut extended play \"The Love Club EP\".\n- On 7 June 2013, Universal Music Group released \"Tennis Court\" as the second single from \"Pure Heroine\", following \"Royals\".\n- In 2013, Lorde later included \"Royals\" on her debut studio album \"Pure Heroine\".\n- In August 2013, \"Royals\" by Lorde topped the chart then named Billboard Alternative Songs.\n- \"Mother Mother\" was the last song by a female solo artist to top that chart before \"Royals\" did so in August 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5a7ea85e-4c70-583d-adf3-9b6a385979c4",
        "text": "Page: Tennis Court (song). Sentence: On 7 June 2013, the song was released as the album's second single by Universal Music Group, following \"Royals\".\nPage: Royals (song). Sentence: \"Royals\" is a song by New Zealand singer Lorde from her debut extended play album, \"The Love Club EP\" (2012).\nPage: Royals (song). Sentence: It was later included on her debut studio album, \"Pure Heroine\" (2013).\nPage: Mother Mother (song). Sentence: It was the last song by a female solo artist to top this chart until \"Royals\" by Lorde in August 2013, by which time the chart had been renamed \"Billboard\" Alternative Songs.",
